Keeps Chromium's priority preferences out of sync. They're a few settings, among them whether to
offer to save passwords, auto sign-in and automatic passkey upgrades, which Chromium syncs in
plain text, so the account's server could write one and change what ilo does. Each device keeps
its own. ilo's settings that follow the account sync as ILO_SETTING, under the passphrase.

--- a/components/sync/base/data_type.h
+++ b/components/sync/base/data_type.h
@@ -352,7 +352,8 @@
           ACCOUNT_SETTING,
           DEVICE_INFO,
           USER_CONSENTS,
-          PRIORITY_PREFERENCES,
+          // browser_core: not PRIORITY_PREFERENCES, which Chromium never
+          // encrypts, so the server could write a setting ilo acts on.
           SECURITY_EVENTS,
           SEND_TAB_TO_SELF,
           SUPERVISED_USER_SETTINGS,
